body:
> Going by https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12356, I suppose your main interest is the C# API? I'm not sure we should be making changes to core based on something that could be solved in C# as well, but I'm open to it if it's the best solution for C#. I suppose we'll need @godotengine/dotnet to comment on that.

The changes are mostly for C#'s benefit (although the `Math::randfn` overload would be accessible through GDExtension as well), but for C# specifically, the changes could definitely be implemented by having methods that look like this:
```cs
public static float Randfn(float mean, float deviation)
{
    return (float)Randfn((double)mean, (double)deviation);
}
```
```cs
public static float RandRange(float from, float to)
{
    return (float)RandRange((double)from, (double)to);
}
```
But that seemed like a hack to me, so I chose not to do it that way. However I am happy to follow your opinion on how the changes should be done.
